{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbHtsy9AdEwsksSyi9gn", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**Banker's rounding** (also called round-half-to-even or round-half-to-even-digit) is a rule for rounding values that fall exactly halfway between two candidates. Instead of always rounding the half up, you round to the nearest **even** digit.\n\n| Value | Round half up | Banker's rounding |\n|-------|---------------|-------------------|\n| 2.5 | 3 | 2 |\n| 3.5 | 4 | 4 |\n| 0.125 \u2192 2 dp | 0.13 | 0.12 |\n| 0.135 \u2192 2 dp | 0.14 | 0.14 |\n\nValues that aren't exactly halfway round the usual way (2.51 \u2192 3, 2.49 \u2192 2).\n\n**Why accountants like it**\n\n- **It removes systematic bias.** Round-half-up always pushes ties upward. Over thousands or millions of transactions, those ties add up to a consistent upward drift in totals. With round-half-even, about half of the ties go up and half go down, because even digits are as likely to be above as below. The errors tend to cancel out.\n- **Aggregates stay closer to the true sum.** This matters when you round many line items, such as interest, tax, or currency conversions, and then add them up. The rounded total is statistically closer to the exact total.\n- **It's fair to both sides.** No party, such as a bank or a customer, gains from the rounding policy over the long run.\n- **It's a standard.** It's the default rounding mode in IEEE 754 floating point, and it's what many financial and accounting systems specify. Examples are Python's `round()`, Java's `RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN`, and .NET's `Math.Round` default.\n\n**Caveats**\n\n- The bias only matters for exact ties. With binary floating point, many \"ties\" like 2.675 aren't exactly representable, so use decimal or integer-cents types for money.\n- Some jurisdictions or contracts require round-half-up, so use whichever rule applies to your case.\n- It's less intuitive. People taught \"5 rounds up\" are often surprised that 2.5 becomes 2."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 6757, "cache_read_input_tokens": 11903, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 6757}, "output_tokens": 4, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "68657c77-0948-40ea-b384-8fad4a192da4", "uuid": "a209be45-30a3-490b-bbfa-89fb9f9dcd2d", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:37:16.020Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbHtsdJVAGtzS6AtrmtV"}
